Package: imputefinder
Title: Condition-Aware Missingness Classification for Proteomics
Version: 0.99.6
Authors@R:
    person("Emir", "Turkes", email = "emir.turkes@eturkes.com",
        role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
        comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-7447-1476"))
Description: Classifies missing protein intensities separately within
    experimental conditions. This can retain condition-specific on/off proteins
    that would be lost when all samples are pooled. Each feature-condition block
    is labelled likely missing-not-at-random (MNAR), likely missing-at-random
    (MAR), complete, insufficient, or absent using observed intensities,
    condition-specific cutoffs, and a strict majority rule. The package accepts
    unnormalised log2 quantitative-proteomics intensities in ordinary matrices
    or SummarizedExperiment objects. It returns filtered data and records the
    classification, cutoff, optional rescue values, original observation
    counts, and drop reason for each feature.
